    "16 / 15 / 17 across bare+import / exemplar / exemplar+rules is one or two tasks at n = 1 per cell, one seed, one model, one fixture. Not a ranking. The only large effect here is bare \u2192 anything that mentions the import.",
    "the fixture is 14 small pure functions with no mocks, no setup and no lifecycle \u2014 the case where a 7B needs the least structural guidance. This says nothing about what an exemplar is worth on real code.",
    "truncate:boundary fails the pass stage in every variant: the fixture's planted off-by-one means a correct boundary assertion is false against the source. It is a constant, not a difference between variants."
